var SPR=[["Summon Giant",6,"Conjuration",["Druid","Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","90 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 hour",1,0,"","Range 90 ft, Concentration 1 hour, 600+ gp slate. Call a giant spirit of a chosen type: Cloud, Fire, Frost, Hill, Stone or Storm. Uses the Giant Spirit stat block.","SUM24",["Druid","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Summon Monstrosity",3,"Conjuration",["Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","90 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 hour",1,0,"","Range 90 ft, Concentration 1 hour, 300+ gp claw. Call a monster spirit: Displacer Beast, Manticore or Owlbear. Uses the Monstrosity Spirit stat block.","SUM24",["Warlock","Wizard"]],["Summon Ooze",4,"Conjuration",["Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","90 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 hour",1,0,"","Range 90 ft, Concentration 1 hour, 400+ gp container. Call an ooze spirit: Gelatinous Cube, Jelly or Oblex. Uses the Ooze Spirit stat block.","SUM24",["Warlock","Wizard"]],["Summon Plant (Summoner class)",3,"Conjuration",["Druid","Ranger"],"Action","90 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 hour",1,0,"","Range 90 ft, Concentration 1 hour, 300+ gp amber plant. Call a plant spirit: Blight, Myconid or Treant. Uses the Plant Spirit stat block.","SUM24",["Druid","Ranger"]],["Summon Titan",9,"Conjuration",[],"Action","90 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 hour",1,0,"","Range 90 ft, Concentration 1 hour, 999+ gp titan remnant. Call a titan spirit: Astral Dreadnought, Kraken or Tarrasque. Uses the Titan Spirit stat block. Casting time 1 action or 10 minutes.","SUM24",[]]];
var SPF={"Summon Giant":"Range 90 ft, Concentration up to 1 hour. Material: a stone slate inscribed with giant runes, worth 600+ gp. You call the glorious spirit of a giant. It appears in an unoccupied space you can see within range and uses the Giant Spirit stat block. When you cast the spell, choose a type: Cloud, Fire, Frost, Hill, Stone or Storm. The creature looks like a giant of that type, which sets some details of its stat block.\n\nThe creature is an ally to you and your allies. In combat it shares your Initiative count but takes its turn right after yours. It obeys your verbal commands with no action from you. If you give none, it takes the Dodge action and moves to avoid danger. It disappears when it drops to 0 Hit Points or when the spell ends.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** Use the level of the slot you spent as the spell's level in the stat block.","Summon Monstrosity":"Range 90 ft, Concentration up to 1 hour. Material: a gilded claw of a Monstrosity worth 300+ gp. You call the essence of a classic monster. It appears in an unoccupied space you can see within range and uses the Monstrosity Spirit stat block. When you cast the spell, choose a form: Displacer Beast, Manticore or Owlbear. The creature looks like a Monstrosity of that kind, which sets some details of its stat block.\n\nThe creature is an ally to you and your allies. In combat it shares your Initiative count but takes its turn right after yours. It obeys your verbal commands with no action from you. If you give none, it takes the Dodge action and moves to avoid danger. It disappears when it drops to 0 Hit Points or when the spell ends.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** Use the level of the slot you spent as the spell's level in the stat block.","Summon Ooze":"Range 90 ft, Concentration up to 1 hour. Material: a container filled with the remains of an ooze, worth 400+ gp. You call the essence of a mindless ooze. It appears in an unoccupied space you can see within range and uses the Ooze Spirit stat block. When you cast the spell, choose a form: Gelatinous Cube, Jelly or Oblex. The creature looks like a formless ooze in a color you pick, and the chosen form sets its traits.\n\nThe creature is an ally to you and your allies. In combat it shares your Initiative count but takes its turn right after yours. It obeys your verbal commands with no action from you. If you give none, it takes the Dodge action and moves to avoid danger. It disappears when it drops to 0 Hit Points or when the spell ends.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** Use the level of the slot you spent as the spell's level in the stat block.","Summon Plant (Summoner class)":"Range 90 ft, Concentration up to 1 hour. Material: a rare plant preserved in amber, worth 300+ gp. You call the spirit of a monstrous grasping plant. It appears in an unoccupied space you can see within range and uses the Plant Spirit stat block. When you cast the spell, choose Blight, Myconid or Treant. The creature looks like a plant creature of that kind, which sets some details of its stat block.\n\nThe creature is an ally to you and your allies. In combat it shares your Initiative count but takes its turn right after yours. It obeys your verbal commands with no action from you. If you give none, it takes the Dodge action and moves to avoid danger. It disappears when it drops to 0 Hit Points or when the spell ends.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** Use the level of the slot you spent as the spell's level in the stat block.","Summon Titan":"Range 90 ft, Concentration up to 1 hour. Casting time: 1 action, or 10 minutes. Casting it as an action gives you 1 level of Exhaustion. Material: a platinum-coated remnant of a Titan, worth 999+ gp. You call the magical form of a Titan. It appears in an unoccupied space you can see within range and uses the Titan Spirit stat block. When you cast the spell, choose a type: Astral Dreadnought, Kraken or Tarrasque. The creature looks like one of that type, which sets some details of its stat block.\n\nThe creature is an ally to you and your allies. In combat it shares your Initiative count but takes its turn right after yours. It obeys your verbal commands with no action from you. If you give none, it takes the Dodge action and moves to avoid danger. It disappears when it drops to 0 Hit Points or when the spell ends."};
var IT=[["Amulet of the Spirit Caller","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"Requires attunement by a spellcaster. The amulet has 5 charges and regains 1d4 + 1 expended charges at dawn. When you cast a summoning spell while wearing it, you can spend charges to boost the summoned creature. Each charge buys one benefit from this list, and you cannot pick the same benefit twice. **Extra Health.** The creature appears with 20 extra Hit Points. **Extra Damage.** It adds 1d4 to each of its damage rolls. **Tougher Hide.** It gains a +2 bonus to AC. Only a spell that needs Concentration and summons a single creature can be boosted this way.",{"by":"a spellcaster","ch":[5,"1d4+1","dawn"]}],["Bands of Synergy","Ring","Rare",1,"Requires attunement by a Summoner. The rings come as a pair. A Summoner wears one and their Eidolon wears the other. While both are worn, the bond between you is stronger. Once per turn, when your Eidolon uses an action that costs Action Points while within 30 ft of you, it can lower the AP cost by 1.",{"by":"a Summoner"}],["Bondmantle","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"Requires attunement by a Summoner. While you wear the mantle, you can take a Magic action to borrow one trait of your Eidolon. Choose one of its skill proficiencies, one of its Speeds, one of its Resistances or Immunities, or one of its senses. You keep the trait until you use the action again.",{"by":"a Summoner"}],["Sphere of the Arcane Armament","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"Requires attunement by a Summoner's Eidolon. This smooth metal lump is soft and easy to shape, yet it slowly settles back into a perfect sphere when left alone. To attune to it, the Eidolon or its Summoner must be holding a magic weapon. Once attuned, that weapon vanishes and the sphere reshapes into a weapon that suits the Eidolon's attacks. Claws give a clawed gauntlet, and a held weapon gives a copy of that weapon. The Eidolon's Conjured Strike gains the magical properties of the absorbed weapon. If that weapon needed attunement, the Eidolon counts as attuned to it without using up one of its attunement slots, and it must still meet any prerequisites. For example, with a Flame Tongue the Eidolon could set its weapon ablaze and deal the extra damage with Conjured Strike. When the attunement ends, the weapon and the sphere reappear within 5 ft of the Eidolon.",{"by":"a Summoner's Eidolon"}],["+1 Soulbind Chains","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"Requires attunement by a Summoner. Wear these fine chains as a necklace or bracelet. They glow faintly while your Eidolon is near. While wearing them, you can use them as a Spellcasting Focus for your spells. You gain a +1 bonus to spell attack rolls and to the saving throw DCs of your Summoner spells. When you give up your action or Bonus Action to grant your Eidolon Action Points, you can raise the Action Points it gains by 2 if it is within 30 ft of you. Once you use this, you cannot use it again until the next dawn.",{"by":"a Summoner"}],["+2 Soulbind Chains","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"Requires attunement by a Summoner. Wear these fine chains as a necklace or bracelet. They glow faintly while your Eidolon is near. While wearing them, you can use them as a Spellcasting Focus for your spells. You gain a +2 bonus to spell attack rolls and to the saving throw DCs of your Summoner spells. When you give up your action or Bonus Action to grant your Eidolon Action Points, you can raise the Action Points it gains by 2 if it is within 30 ft of you. Once you use this, you cannot use it again until the next dawn.",{"by":"a Summoner"}],["+3 Soulbind Chains","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"Requires attunement by a Summoner. Wear these fine chains as a necklace or bracelet. They glow faintly while your Eidolon is near. While wearing them, you can use them as a Spellcasting Focus for your spells. You gain a +3 bonus to spell attack rolls and to the saving throw DCs of your Summoner spells. When you give up your action or Bonus Action to grant your Eidolon Action Points, you can raise the Action Points it gains by 2 if it is within 30 ft of you. Once you use this, you cannot use it again until the next dawn.",{"by":"a Summoner"}],["Evolution Stone (Rare)","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"If a Summoner's Eidolon holds this stone for 24 hours, it permanently gains one Evolution, even if it does not meet the prerequisites. If it already knows that Evolution, it can instead swap it at once for another Evolution whose prerequisites it meets. The stone then becomes a mundane crystal worth 1d4 x 100 gp.",{}],["Evolution Stone (Very Rare)","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",0,"If a Summoner's Eidolon holds this stone for 24 hours, it permanently gains one Evolution, even if it does not meet the prerequisites. If it already knows that Evolution, it can instead swap it at once for another Evolution whose prerequisites it meets. The stone then becomes a mundane crystal worth 1d4 x 100 gp.",{}],["Evolution Stone (Legendary)","Wondrous Item","Legendary",0,"If a Summoner's Eidolon holds this stone for 24 hours, it permanently gains one Evolution, even if it does not meet the prerequisites. If it already knows that Evolution, it can instead swap it at once for another Evolution whose prerequisites it meets. The stone then becomes a mundane crystal worth 1d4 x 100 gp.",{}]];
